stimated savings.</p></div><div class=\"panel stack\"><div><label>Vehicle Price (PKR)</label><input type=\"number\" id=\"discountPrice\" value=\"41800000\" min=\"0\"></div><div><label>Promo Code</label><input id=\"discountCode\" placeholder=\"e.g. WELCOME5\"></div><button class=\"btn\" onclick=\"discount()\">Apply Code ↗</button><div id=\"discountResult\"></div></div></div></section>`;\n47: const discount=()=>{let n=+document.getElementById('discountPrice').value,code=document.getElementById('discountCode').value.trim().toUpperCase(),rate={WELCOME5:.05,APEX10:.1,VIP15:.15}[code];document.getElementById('discountResult').innerHTML=n>0&&rate?`<div class=\"notice\">You save ${money(n*rate)}. Estimated total: <strong>${money(n*(1-rate))}</strong></div>`:'<div class=\"notice error\">Enter a valid price and promo code.</div>'};\n48: const reviews=()=>{let r=get('reviews',[{name:'Ayesha K.',rating:5,comment:'Beautiful showroom experience and a seamless way to explore luxury cars.'},{name:'Hamza R.',rating:5,comment:'The comparison tool made choosing between models much easier.'},{name:'Sara M.',rating:4,comment:'Clean design and a very intuitive booking process.'}]);return hero('The APEX Experience.','Stories from our showroom community. Demo reviews shown below.')+section('What Drivers Are Saying','Explore visitor impressions and share your own.',`<div class=\"grid\">${r.map(x=>`<div class=\"panel\"><div class=\"review-stars\">${'★'.repeat(x.rating)}${'☆'.repeat(5-x.rating)}</div><p style=\"margin-top:20px\">“${escapeHtml(x.comment)}”</p><strong>${escapeHtml(x.name)}</strong></div>`).join('')}</div>`)+`<section class=\"section alt\"><div class=\"wrap\" style=\"max-width:750px\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">SHARE YOUR EXPERIENCE</div><h2>Leave a Review.</h2><form class=\"panel stack\" onsubmit=\"submitReview(event)\"><div><label>Your Name</label><input name=\"name\" required minlength=\"2\"></div><div><label>Rating</label><select name=\"rating\" required><option value=\"5\">★★★★★ Excellent</option><option value=\"4\">★★★★ Very Good</option><option value=\"3\">★★★ Good</option><option value=\"2\">★★ Fair</option><option value=\"1\">★ Poor</option></select></div><div><label>Your Review</label><textarea name=\"comment\" required minlength=\"10\" rows=\"4\"></textarea></div><button class=\"btn\">Submit Review ↗</button></form></div></section>`};\n49: const escapeHtml=s=>String(s).replace(/[&<>\"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;',\"'\":'&#39;'}[c]));\n50: const submitReview=e=>{e.preventDefault();let d=Object.fromEntries(new FormData(e.target));let r=get('reviews',[]);r.push({...d,rating:+d.rating});set('reviews',r);toast('Review submitted');render()};\n51: const saved=()=>hero('Your Private Collection.','Keep your favorite vehicles close. Your wishlist stays saved in this browser.')+section('Saved Vehicles','The extraordinary models you have chosen to remember.',cards(cars().filter(c=>wish().includes(c.id)))+'<div style=\"margin-top:28px\"><a class=\"btn outline\" href=\"'+href('explore-cars')+'\">Explore More Vehicles ↗</a></div>');\n52: const about=()=>hero('Driven by Passion.','A vision to make extraordinary automobiles more accessible to discover and experience.')+`<section class=\"section\"><div class=\"wrap split\"><img src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1493238792000-8113da705763?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1100&q=85\" alt=\"Luxury automotive showroom\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">OUR STORY</div><h2>More Than a Showroom.</h2><p>APEX MOTORS is a fictional premium automotive showroom concept, built around a simple idea: the journey to your next car should be as inspiring as the car itself.</p><p>Our digital experience brings together carefully curated vehicles, clear specifications and thoughtful tools for discovery, comparison and planning.</p><a class=\"btn\" href=\"${href('explore-cars')}\">Discover the Collection ↗</a></div></div></section>${section('Our Guiding Principles','Everything we do is inspired by a passion for automotive excellence.',`<div class=\"grid\">${[['01','Our Mission','Make discovering premium vehicles effortless, inspiring and informative.'],['02','Our Vision','Create a digital showroom experience that feels truly exceptional.'],['03','Our Promise','Clarity, elegant design and a seamless experience at every step.']].map(x=>`<div class=\"panel\"><div class=\"number\">${x[0]}</div><h3>${x[1]}</h3><p>${x[2]}</p></div>`).join('')}</div>`,true)}`;\n53: const contact=()=>hero('Let’s Connect.','Questions, inquiries or feedback? We would love to hear from you.')+`<section class=\"section\"><div class=\"wrap details-layout\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">CONTACT OUR TEAM</div><h2>Every Great Journey Starts with a Conversation.</h2><p>This is a demo showroom. Contact form messages are stored locally in your browser, not sent to a real dealership.</p><div class=\"panel\"><h3>Our Showroom Concept</h3><p>Islamabad, Pakistan</p><p>Opening Hours: Mon–Sat · 10:00 AM–7:00 PM (illustrative)</p><a class=\"link\" href=\"${href('faq')}\">Frequently Asked Questions ↗</a></div></div><form class=\"panel form-grid\" onsubmit=\"submitContact(event)\"><div><label>Your Name *</label><input name=\"name\" required minlength=\"2\"></div><div><label>Email *</label><input type=\"email\" name=\"email\" required></div><div class=\"wide\"><label>Subject *</label><select name=\"subject\" required><option>General Inquiry</option><option>Vehicle Availability</option><option>Test Drive</option><option>Financing</option></select></div><div class=\"wide\"><label>Message *</label><textarea name=\"message\" required minlength=\"10\" rows=\"6\"></textarea></div><div class=\"wide\"><button class=\"btn\">Send Demo Message ↗</button><p class=\"small-text\">No email will actually be sent.</p></div></form></div></section>`;\n54: const submitContact=e=>{e.preventDefault();let a=get('messages',[]);a.push(Object.fromEntries(new FormData(e.target)));set('messages',a);e.target.reset();toast('Message saved locally')};\n55: const faq=()=>hero('Here to Help.','Answers to common questions about discovering and experiencing our vehicles.')+`<section class=\"section\"><div class=\"wrap details-layout\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS</div><h2>Everything You Need to Know.</h2><p>Find answers to questions about our collection, demo bookings and ownership planning.</p><a class=\"btn\" href=\"${href('contact')}\">Still Have Questions? ↗</a></div><div class=\"panel\">${[['How do I book a test drive?','Select a vehicle and complete the test-drive form. This concept website stores demo bookings in your browser.'],['Can I compare two vehicles?','Yes. Add vehicles to the comparison list or select them on the Compare Cars page.'],['Are the displayed prices final?','No. All prices are illustrative sample values for this academic showroom concept.'],['How does the finance calculator work?','It estimates monthly payments using the loan amount, annual interest rate and duration.'],['Where are my saved cars stored?','Your wishlist is stored locally in this browser using localStorage.'],['Can I purchase a vehicle here?','No. This is a demonstration showroom website, not a live dealership.']].map(x=>`<details class=\"faq-item\"><summary>${x[0]}</summary><p>${x[1]}</p></details>`).join('')}</div></div></section><section class=\"section alt\"><div class=\"wrap details-layout\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">OWNERSHIP PLANNING</div><h2>Estimate Your Annual Costs.</h2><p>Adjust the figures to get a rough estimate of annual running costs.</p></div><div class=\"panel stack\"><div><label>Monthly Fuel / Charging Cost (PKR)</label><input id=\"fuel\" type=\"number\" value=\"40000\" min=\"0\"></div><div><label>Annual Insurance (PKR)</label><input id=\"insurance\" type=\"number\" value=\"250000\" min=\"0\"></div><div><label>Annual Maintenance (PKR)</label><input id=\"maintenance\" type=\"number\" value=\"180000\" min=\"0\"></div><button class=\"btn\" onclick=\"ownership()\">Calculate Annual Cost ↗</button><div id=\"ownershipResult\"></div></div></div></section>`;\n56: const ownership=()=>{let a=['fuel','insurance','maintenance'].map(id=>+document.getElementById(id).value);document.getElementById('ownershipResult').innerHTML=a.some(x=>x<0)?'<div class=\"notice error\">Costs cannot be negative.</div>':`<div class=\"notice\">Estimated yearly running cost: <strong>${money(a[0]*12+a[1]+a[2])}</strong></div>`};\n57: const admin=()=>{let b=bookings(),c=cars();return hero('The Command Center.','Your showroom, at a glance. All data is local to this browser.','APEX MOTORS / ADMIN')+`<section class=\"section\"><div class=\"wrap\"><div class=\"grid four\">${[[c.length,'Total Vehicles'],[b.length,'Total Bookings'],[b.filter(x=>x.status==='Pending').length,'Pending Requests'],[b.filter(x=>x.status==='Approved').length,'Approved Bookings']].map(x=>`<div class=\"stat\"><strong>${x[0]}</strong><span>${x[1]}</span></div>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"grid two\" style=\"margin-top:28px\"><a class=\"panel\" href=\"${href('inventory')}\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">SHOWROOM OPERATIONS</div><h2>Manage Inventory ↗</h2><p>Add, edit and remove vehicles in your local demo catalogue.</p></a><a class=\"panel\" href=\"${href('bookings')}\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">CUSTOMER EXPERIENCES</div><h2>Manage Bookings ↗</h2><p>Review and update test-drive requests.</p></a></div><div class=\"panel\" style=\"margin-top:28px\"><h3>Collection by Brand</h3>${[...new Set(c.map(x=>x.brand))].map(brand=>`<div class=\"row\"><span>${brand}</span><strong>${c.filter(x=>x.brand===brand).length} vehicles</strong></div><div class=\"progress\"><span style=\"width:${c.filter(x=>x.brand===brand).length/c.length*100}%\"></span></div>`).join('')}</div></div></section>`};\n58: const inventory=()=>hero('Manage Inventory.','Add, edit or remove vehicles. Changes are saved locally.','APEX MOTORS / ADMIN')+`<section class=\"section\"><div class=\"wrap\"><div class=\"panel\"><h3 id=\"inventoryHeading\">Add Vehicle</h3><form id=\"inventoryForm\" class=\"form-grid\" onsubmit=\"saveVehicle(event)\"><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"id\" id=\"editId\"><div><label>Brand *</label><input name=\"brand\" required></div><div><label>Model *</label><input name=\"model\" required></div><div><label>Price (PKR) *</label><input type=\"number\" name=\"price\" min=\"1\" required></div><div><label>Year *</label><input type=\"number\" name=\"year\" min=\"1990\" max=\"2035\" required></div><div><label>Engine *</label><input name=\"engine\" required></div><div><label>Power *</label><input name=\"power\" required></div><div><label>0–100 km/h *</label><input name=\"speed\" required></div><div><label>Body Type *</label><input name=\"type\" required></div><div class=\"wide\"><label>Image URL *</label><input name=\"img\" type=\"url\" required placeholder=\"https://...\"></div><div class=\"wide\"><button class=\"btn\">Save Vehicle ↗</button> <button type=\"reset\" class=\"btn ghost\" onclick=\"document.getElementById('editId').value='';document.getElementById('inventoryHeading').textContent='Add Vehicle'\">Clear</button></div></form></div><div class=\"panel\" style=\"margin-top:30px\"><h3>Current Inventory</h3><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"table\"><thead><tr><th>Vehicle</th><th>Year</th><th>Price</th><th>Actions</th></tr></thead><tbody>${cars().map(c=>`<tr><td>${escapeHtml(c.brand)} ${escapeHtml(c.model)}</td><td>${c.year}</td><td>${money(c.price)}</td><td><button class=\"btn small outline\" onclick=\"editVehicle(${c.id})\">Edit</button> <button class=\"btn small ghost\" onclick=\"deleteVehicle(${c.id})\">Delete</button></td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div></div></div></section>`;\n59: const saveVehicle=e=>{e.preventDefault();let d=Object.fromEntries(new FormData(e.target)),a=cars();d.price=Number(d.price);d.year=Number(d.year);d.id=d.id?Number(d.id):Date.now();d.tag='Available';if(a.some(c=>c.id===d.id))a=a.map(c=>c.id===d.id?d:c);else a.push(d);set('cars',a);toast('Vehicle saved');render()};\n60: const editVehicle=id=>{let c=car(id),f=document.getElementById('inventoryForm');Object.keys(c).forEach(k=>{if(f.elements[k])f.elements[k].value=c[k]});document.getElementById('inventoryHeading').textContent='Edit Vehicle';window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})};\n61: const deleteVehicle=id=>{if(confirm('Remove this vehicle from inventory?')){set('cars',cars().filter(c=>c.id!==id));toast('Vehicle removed');render()}};\n62: const manageBookings=()=>hero('Manage Bookings.','Review and manage customer test-drive requests.','APEX MOTORS / ADMIN')+`<section class=\"section\"><div class=\"wrap\"><div class=\"panel\"><div class=\"row\"><h3>Booking Records</h3><span class=\"pill\">${bookings().length} Requests</span></div><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"table\"><thead><tr><th>Customer</th><th>Vehicle</th><th>Date / Time</th><th>Status</th><th>Actions</th></tr></thead><tbody>${bookings().length?bookings().map(b=>`<tr><td>${escapeHtml(b.first)} ${escapeHtml(b.last)}<div class=\"meta\">${escapeHtml(b.email)}</div></td><td>${escapeHtml(b.car)}</td><td>${b.date}<div class=\"meta\">${b.time}</div></td><td><span class=\"pill\">${b.status}</span></td><td><select aria-label=\"Update booking status\" onchange=\"updateBooking(${b.id},this.value)\">${['Pending','Approved','Rejected','Completed'].map(s=>`<option ${b.status===s?'selected':''}>${s}</option>`).join('')}</select><button class=\"btn small ghost\" onclick=\"removeBooking(${b.id})\">Delete</button></td></tr>`).join(''):'<tr><td colspan=\"5\" class=\"muted\">No test-drive bookings yet. Submit a demo booking to see it here.</td></tr>'}</tbody></table></div></div></div></section>`;\n63: const updateBooking=(id,status)=>{set('bookings',bookings().map(b=>b.id===id?{...b,status}:b));toast('Booking status updated');render()};\n64: const removeBooking=id=>{if(confirm('Delete this booking?')){set('bookings',bookings().filter(b=>b.id!==id));render()}};\n65: const views={'index':home,'explore-cars':explore,'car-details':details,'compare-cars':compare,'finance-calculator':finance,'test-drive':testDrive,'brands':brands,'brand-collection':brandCollection,'new-arrivals':arrivals,'offers':offers,'reviews':reviews,'saved-cars':saved,'about':about,'contact':contact,'faq':faq,'admin':admin,'inventory':inventory,'bookings':manageBookings};\n66: function render(){document.getElementById('app').innerHTML=header()+(views[page]||home)()+footer();if(page==='compare-cars')renderComparison();if(page==='finance-calculator')calcFinance();if(page==='test-drive'){document.getElementById('driveDate').min=new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-CA')}}\n67: function filterCars(){let q=document.getElementById('search').value.toLowerCase(),b=document.getElementById('brand').value,t=document.getElementById('type').value,s=document.getElementById('sort').value;let a=cars().filter(c=>(c.brand+' '+c.model).toLowerCase().includes(q)&&(!b||c.brand===b)&&(!t||c.type===t));if(s==='low')a.sort((x,y)=>x.price-y.price);if(s==='high')a.sort((x,y)=>y.price-x.price);if(s==='new')a.sort((x,y)=>y.year-x.year);document.getElementById('results').innerHTML=cards(a);document.getElementById('count').textContent=a.length+' exceptional vehicles'}\n68: function subscribe(e){e.preventDefault();let email=e.target.querySelector('input').value,a=get('subscribers',[]);if(!a.includes(email))a.push(email);set('subscribers',a);e.target.reset();toast('Subscribed to demo newsletter')}\n69: render();"}
{"step_index":48,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-26T10:43:18Z","model":"gemini-4-hydrogen-high","input_tokens":33828,"cache_read_tokens":36791,"output_tokens":5371,"content":"I have carefully read [CL1000_Final_Project (1).pdf](file:///C:/Users/User/OneDrive/Desktop/CarVault%20project/CL1000_Final_Project%20(1).pdf) along with the sample [index.html](file:///C:/Users/User/OneDrive/Desktop/CarVault%20project/index.html), [css/style.css](file:///C:/Users/User/OneDrive/Desktop/CarVault%20project/css/style.css), and [js/app.js](file:///C:/Users/User/OneDrive/Desktop/CarVault%20project/js/app.js).\n\nHere are the **key CL1000 rules** I will make sure we follow:\n1. **Exactly your 3 pages** (`index.html`, `pages/explore-cars.html`, `pages/car-details.html`) in the required `index.html`, `pages/`, `css/`, `js/`, `images/`, `docs/` structure—keeping all navbar links from your prototype ready for your teammates' pages.\n2. **Original, explainable code (no template copy):** We will **not** reuse the minified APEX MOTORS `app.js` or branding. Every HTML, CSS, and Vanilla JS file will be written cleanly with simple comments so you can understand and explain every line (and make live changes) during your **Demo & Viva**.\n3. **All 6 CL1000 Feature Categories + Feature Depth:**\n   * **Data & Display:** Central JS car catalog (`cars-data.js`), dynamic Featured Cars, Search, Brand/Price/Type Filters, Sorting, and dynamic Car Details (`?id=...`).\n   * **Forms & Input:** Your **4-State Test Drive Booking Flow** (Empty -> Filled -> Success / Failed `\"Incorrect phone no. or e-mail. Please enter again.\"` + `\"Try Again\"`).\n   * **State & Memory:** `localStorage` Wishlist (`♡ Wishlist` + navbar `Saved Cars` viewer) and saved booking requests across reloads.\n   * **Interaction:** Car Details thumbnail gallery switcher, booking flow modal, Saved Cars modal, mobile hamburger menu, collapsible mobile filter panel.\n   * **Logic & Calculation:** PKR price-bracket filtering (`Rs. 10 lac – 50 lac`, `Rs. 50 lac – 1 Cr`, `Rs. 1 Cr & above`), sorting, dynamic result counts, plus a small, clean **Estimated Monthly Installment** calculator on Car Details so this category is strongly covered.\n   * **Responsive & Accessible:** Mobile Home layout matching Sketch ④, responsive Explore & Details pages, semantic `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<footer>`, `alt` attributes, and keyboard focus styling.\n4. **AI Image Disclosure (Rule 11):** If we generate local car/logo images in `images/`, we will add the required disclosure in the footer (`\"Images on this website were generated using ...\"`).\n5. **README, Git & Logs:**\n   * `README.md` will keep the existing title and add the required **Feature Table** (`Feature | Category | Page | Member`) and **Contribution Table**.\n   * We will make meaningful commits on branch `26i3054` (remember: the rubric requires commits spread across **at least 3 days** before **Sunday, 29th Nov 2026, 11:59 pm**, and you will export your Antigravity CLI session logs into `docs/ai-logs/<your-roll-number>/` untouched).\n\n---\n\n### Before I Make Any Changes, Please Confirm:\n1. **Replace sample files & organize photos:** May I replace the APEX MOTORS sample [index.html](file:///C:/Users/User/OneDrive/Desktop/CarVault%20project/index.html), [css/style.css](file:///C:/Users/User/OneDrive/Desktop/CarVault%20project/css/style.css), and [js/app.js](file:///C:/Users/User/OneDrive/Desktop/CarVault%20project/js/app.js) with our clean **CAR VAULT** code, and move your 3 prototype `.jpeg` files into `docs/prototype-photos/`?\n2. **Teammate navbar links (`Brands`, `New`, `Offers`, `About`, `Contact`, `Compare`):** Should these point to `pages/brands.html`, `pages/new-arrivals.html`, `pages/offers.html`, `pages/about.html`, `pages/contact.html`, `pages/compare-cars.html` so they connect automatically once your teammates merge their branches (while `Home`, `Explore`, `Test Drive`, and `Saved Cars` work right away)?\n3. **Images:** Should I generate clean local car, hero, and logo images inside `images/` so nothing ever fails to load offline or on GitHub Pages?\n4. **Your details for `README.md` & `docs/`:** What is your **full name** and **roll number** (looks like `26I-3054` from your branch name)?\n\nReply **\"Go ahead\"** with those quick answers, and I will start building!","thinking":"Reviewing the project guidelines and existing code reveals the core structural requirements. The current assumption that pages can be distributed arbitrarily conflicts with the mandate requiring each student to implement precisely three specific pages. Shifting focus to verify page allocations and match them against the prototype definitions.\n\nDiscarding the template's minified assets and branding to prevent plagiarism risks and viva complications. Building custom, well-commented vanilla code tailored specifically to the three-page scope rather than adapting the generic multi-page sample.\n\nNavigation items need full representation to match prototype completeness, yet unassigned teammate links risk appearing broken during evaluation. Directing inactive teammate routes to placeholder states prevents dead links while preserving structural alignment with the required directory layout.\n\nMandatory artifact folders require careful handling, particularly regarding local image assets and strict prohibitions against fabricating session logs or compliance reports. Documenting team contributions and feature distribution across required categories ensures alignment with the evaluation criteria.\n\nImplementing dynamic array-driven rendering for the catalog and featured items establishes the core display logic. Incorporating the four-state test drive validation flow alongside local storage persistence secures user state across sessions. Adding price bracket parsing and sorting logic satisfies the quantitative requirements for the explorer view.\n\nWeighing whether to embed an interactive finance calculator or keep the primary vehicle details strictly aligned with the prototype views. Re-evaluating the multi-page linking strategy to ensure all teammate routes exist as functional placeholders while restricting active implementation strictly to the assigned three pages. Factoring the multi-day commit timeline into the deployment strategy to satisfy project distribution rules.\n\nInterpreting the ambiguous directive regarding navigation items as a requirement to preserve all prototype navbar links and statistics boxes across the layout. Mapping inactive teammate routes to corresponding placeholder files ensures navigation remains intact without exceeding the assigned three-page implementation boundary.\n\nRecognizing the explicit instruction to withhold code modifications until receiving formal approval. Pausing implementation to present the refined strategy and request final confirmation before altering repository files.\n\nFinalizing the file architecture around the specified directory tree, color scheme, and distinct modules. Confirmed the strict adherence to original, well-commented vanilla scripts over external templates to mitigate viva risks.\n\nIntegrating the remaining feature categories into the architecture, ensuring the local storage wishlist, interactive car details gallery, and PKR-based pricing filters satisfy the logic and calculation requirements. Factoring in the mandated inclusion of physical chart photos and proper asset disclosures to fulfill the Phase assessment criteria.\n\n"}
